/E (Some processes exist in pieces. Others don't exist at all. When you're operating across dozens of people and thousands of external partners, the common thread is usually the same - nothing lives in a system. It lives in people's heads. The people running it have adapted around its flaws for so long that the flaws feel normal. Asking questions can feel threatening, and the answers you get are often incomplete.)
